(Evaluation of an Alternative Costimulation-Blocking Strategy for Preventing Psoriasis) Tj
T*
(Recurrence Following Biologic Agent Withdrawal: A Randomized Controlled Protocol) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Alternative biologic therapies target different pathogenic pathways in psoriasis, and) Tj
T*
(transitioning between agents may offer clinical advantages. This protocol describes a) Tj
T*
(double-blind, placebo-controlled randomized trial investigating whether costimulatory) Tj
T*
(blockade with an alternative biologic can maintain psoriasis control after withdrawal of a) Tj
T*
(first-line biologic therapy. Adults with moderate-to-severe plaque psoriasis who) Tj
T*
(demonstrate response to an initial biologic agent will enter a lead-in phase. Those) Tj
T*
(achieving clinical improvement are then randomly assigned to either continue the original) Tj
T*
(biologic therapy or switch to an alternative costimulatory-blocking agent, with both) Tj
T*
(maintained through mid-study then withdrawn. The primary outcome is proportion of) Tj
T*
(participants experiencing disease relapse over subsequent follow-up. Secondary endpoints) Tj
T*
(assess time to relapse and molecular disease markers. We hypothesize the alternative) Tj
T*
(mechanism of action will sustain clinical benefit comparable to continued original) Tj
T*
(therapy.) Tj
